1
00:00:00,594 --> 00:00:02,269
Watch someone's eyes, and you know what they're

2
00:00:02,269 --> 00:00:03,342
thinking about.

3
00:00:03,342 --> 00:00:06,348
Every glance, every blink, says something.

4
00:00:06,554 --> 00:00:08,110
That's why machines are learning to read our

5
00:00:08,110 --> 00:00:11,224
eyes. A headset sharpens only where you look.

6
00:00:11,224 --> 00:00:13,959
A car warns a driver whose eyes leave the road.

7
00:00:13,959 --> 00:00:16,165
People who can't speak type with their eyes.

8
00:00:16,165 --> 00:00:19,571
And a child's gaze can help doctors spot autism early.

9
00:00:20,566 --> 00:00:22,476
Every one of these systems has to learn from

10
00:00:22,476 --> 00:00:25,931
real faces, with eyes that move like real eyes.

11
00:00:25,931 --> 00:00:27,382
Filming people is slow

12
00:00:27,382 --> 00:00:28,856
expensive and private.

13
00:00:28,856 --> 00:00:30,849
And most digital eyes look dead

14
00:00:30,849 --> 00:00:33,536
glassy, staring and robotic.

15
00:00:33,730 --> 00:00:36,832
This is Synthetic Eyes, built on Google's GNM

16
00:00:36,832 --> 00:00:39,803
head, by Team Rocklef from SRM Institute of

17
00:00:39,803 --> 00:00:41,524
Science and Technology.

18
00:00:42,118 --> 00:00:44,889
Researchers built 3D head models like FLAME and

19
00:00:44,889 --> 00:00:47,696
GNM, and eye tools like UnityEyes.

20
00:00:47,696 --> 00:00:49,972
But the head models come without lifelike skin

21
00:00:49,972 --> 00:00:53,119
or eyes, and the eye tools only show the eye.

22
00:00:53,325 --> 00:00:56,403
So we gave GNM photoreal skin, living eyes and

23
00:00:56,403 --> 00:00:57,535
natural motion

24
00:00:57,535 --> 00:01:00,045
all driven by one Python script.

25
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:02,999
Every texture is painted straight onto GNM's own

26
00:01:02,999 --> 00:01:06,537
UV map, so it wraps onto the head with no seams.

27
00:01:06,537 --> 00:01:09,190
Eight faces, of different ages and backgrounds

28
00:01:09,190 --> 00:01:12,138
with pores, freckles, wrinkles, and eyebrows

29
00:01:12,138 --> 00:01:13,741
drawn hair by hair.

30
00:01:13,935 --> 00:01:17,142
Each eye gets its own 4K iris, with fibres

31
00:01:17,142 --> 00:01:18,947
crypts and a ring of colour

32
00:01:18,947 --> 00:01:21,304
and a pupil that really traps the light.

33
00:01:21,510 --> 00:01:23,149
Then we check our own work

34
00:01:23,149 --> 00:01:25,590
every UV seam on the head is measured against

35
00:01:25,590 --> 00:01:27,465
the skin's natural detail.

36
00:01:27,465 --> 00:01:29,044
All eight sets pass.

37
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:32,080
Type Left, Right, or Generate Motion, and the

38
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:34,757
script renders the frames and the video.

39
00:01:34,757 --> 00:01:37,741
The eyes jump at real human speeds, settle

40
00:01:37,741 --> 00:01:39,274
drift, and blink

41
00:01:39,274 --> 00:01:41,573
fast to close, slower to open.

42
00:01:41,573 --> 00:01:43,012
The head follows a little

43
00:01:43,012 --> 00:01:45,109
and the eyelids follow the eyes.

44
00:01:45,316 --> 00:01:47,438
The blend file plays a whole expression on

45
00:01:47,438 --> 00:01:48,771
Blender's timeline

46
00:01:48,771 --> 00:01:51,919
surprise, a suspicious squint and an eye roll

47
00:01:51,919 --> 00:01:55,420
with eyelids, pupils and brows moving together.

48
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:58,586
Change the face with GNM's own shape sliders

49
00:01:58,586 --> 00:02:01,179
and the eyes stay perfectly in place.

50
00:02:01,374 --> 00:02:02,282
Under the hood

51
00:02:02,282 --> 00:02:05,678
GNM rebuilt in Python, expressions solved inside

52
00:02:05,678 --> 00:02:07,482
GNM's own eye space

53
00:02:07,482 --> 00:02:09,664
textures baked through its UV map

54
00:02:09,664 --> 00:02:11,268
and a control wrapper to look

55
00:02:11,268 --> 00:02:13,353
open the eyelids and blink.

56
00:02:13,548 --> 00:02:15,163
Compared with today's tools

57
00:02:15,163 --> 00:02:17,722
ours gives a whole photoreal face, a separate

58
00:02:17,722 --> 00:02:20,659
iris for each eye, human motion over time

59
00:02:20,659 --> 00:02:22,768
and eyelids that follow the gaze.

60
00:02:22,974 --> 00:02:25,840
That opens the door to lifelike avatars, safer

61
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:29,341
cars, better eye trackers, and medical research.

62
00:02:29,547 --> 00:02:32,294
Next, we'll carry the textures over to FLAME

63
00:02:32,294 --> 00:02:34,853
add infrared headset cameras, and run it all in

64
00:02:34,853 --> 00:02:36,019
real time.

65
00:02:36,214 --> 00:02:38,171
Want the code, or to build on it?

66
00:02:38,171 --> 00:02:41,201
Email us. Thank you, from Team Rocklef.

